  "interpretation": "Chrome emitted a trusted pointercancel and non-cancelable touchmove. It occurred both near the bottom controls and after the same item was fully revealed by real scrolling, so bottom-edge occlusion alone does not explain it. The sparse-input attempts did not deliver to OH; UI drag state cleaned up. Continuous 6px / 16ms touch samples successfully delivered the same scrolled item, retained in the final report. This observation does not establish a universal browser cause or claim a production fix.",
